@*
    ONE TASK ON THE BOARD - story 2.2, AC6; UX-DR8; DESIGN.md:137-144, :389-453.

    THE TITLE IS THE ONLY CONTENT. A metadata row in monospace sits beneath it and is empty in 2.2: Labels
    (2.4), the Assignee (4.6) and Presence (Epic 7) fill it, so nothing stands in for them here - no
    placeholder, no count, no badge, no streak (engagement is a counter-metric).

    NOT A CONTROL YET. No click target (the detail panel is 2.3), not focusable (the keyboard grid is 2.8),
    and no drag handle or Move control for any Role (2.7, 2.6). The card carries no shadow, declared
    explicitly in components.css so nobody adds one back.
*@

<li class="task-card">
    <p class="type-task-title task-card__title">@Title</p>
    <div class="type-meta task-card__meta"></div>
</li>

@code {
    /// <summary>The Task's title, rendered as text.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    [EditorRequired]
    public string Title { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}
